n 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\", \"quote\": \"The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-13", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"found\": true, \"answer\": \"The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\", \"quote\": \"Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-13", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"found\": true, \"answer\": \"The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\", \"quote\": \"The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-13", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"found\": false, \"answer\": \"\", \"quote\": \"\"}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-13", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "reasoning":